error[E0083]: 'Box' literal omits field(s) with no zero value: 'r'
  --> error_enum_no_zero_value.bit:20:11
   |
20 |   let b = Box{}
   |           ^^^^^ a class-typed field is a reference and would be null; a payload-carrying enum's zero tag names a variant that has no payload to give it — give each one a value (§13.4)
error[E0083]: 'Result<i64, string>' cannot be default-constructed: its zero tag names 'Ok', which carries a payload and has no zero value
  --> error_enum_no_zero_value.bit:23:7
   |
23 |   let x: Result<int, string>
   |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ give the binding an initializer, e.g. `= Result<i64, string>.<variant>(...)` (§13.4)
error[E0083]: 'Result<i64, string>' has no zero value, so '[]Result<i64, string>(2)' cannot fill its elements: its zero tag names 'Ok', which carries a payload
  --> error_enum_no_zero_value.bit:26:12
   |
26 |   let xs = []Result<int, string>(2)
   |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ build the slice from values instead, e.g. `[]Result<i64, string>{ ... }`, or start from `[]Result<i64, string>(0)` and append (§13.4)
error[E0083]: 'Box' has no zero value, so '[]Box(2)' cannot fill its elements: field(s) with no zero value: 'r'
  --> error_enum_no_zero_value.bit:29:12
   |
29 |   let bs = []Box(2)
   |            ^^^^^^^^ build the slice from values instead, e.g. `[]Box{ ... }`, or start from `[]Box(0)` and append (§13.4)
error[E0083]: 'Box' cannot be default-constructed: field(s) with no zero value: 'r'
  --> error_enum_no_zero_value.bit:32:7
   |
32 |   let y: Box
   |       ^^^^^^ give the binding an initializer naming them, e.g. `= Box{ ... }` (§13.4)
